# Overlays

- Each overlay is a widget in `lib/overlays/` that takes `final FlappyActionGame game` in its constructor.
- Register every overlay in `main.dart`'s `overlayBuilderMap`. The key is the overlay name used everywhere else (`mainMenu`, `pauseMenu`, `gameOverMenu`, `countdown`).
- Lay out on a 10×10 grid with `LayoutBuilder`, matching the existing overlays:

```dart
final gridX = constraints.maxWidth / 10;
final gridY = constraints.maxHeight / 10;
```

- Use `SpriteWidget(sprite: SpriteUtil.…)` for buttons and titles; wrap content in `SafeArea`.
- Button handlers call one `game.<method>()` (`startGame`, `resumeGame`, `restartGame`, `goToMainMenu`, …). Do not call `game.overlays.add/remove`, `pauseEngine`, or `resumeEngine` from an overlay — add a method to `FlappyActionGame` instead.
- Dimmed modal overlays use a full-screen `Container(color: Colors.black.withAlpha(…))` under the content, like `PauseMenu`.
